<title>KAZAKHSTAN: Kazakh non-CIS Jan-Apr trade surplus narrows.</title>
<headline>Kazakh non-CIS Jan-Apr trade surplus narrows.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kazakhstan's trade surplus with non-CIS countries narrowed to $641.1 million in the first four months of this year from $643.0 million in the same period of 1996, the State Statistics Committee said on Monday.</p>
<p>It gave the following data:</p>
<p>		KAZAKHSTAN NON-CIS MERCHANDISE TRADE</p>
<p>    (millions of dollars)   Jan-Apr 97  Jan-Apr 96</p>
<p>    Exports			 1,139.4	 963.1</p>
<p>    Imports			   498.3	 320.1</p>
<p>    Trade balance		  +641.1	+643.0</p>
<p>Note: Trade with countries of the Commonwealth of Independent States, not included in this table, accounts for 56 percent of the Central Asian country's imports and 44 percent of exports.</p>
<p>--Almaty Newsroom, +7 3272 509410</p>
</text>
